From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] journal: stop bailing out before the main view gets a canvas

show_main_view() opens with the correct guard - skip the rebuild when MAIN is
already the active view *and* already the canvas - but it was followed by six
identical bare copies:

    if self._active_view == JournalViews.MAIN:
        return

Those return whenever the active view is MAIN regardless of whether the canvas
was ever set. _active_view starts as MAIN, so the first call during _setup()
returned before reaching set_canvas(self._main_view) and the Journal was left
permanently blank: pressing F5 produced an empty white surface with no
toolbar, search or entries.

Removing the bare duplicates leaves the original compound guard, which is the
one that was written to be correct.

--- a/src/jarabe/journal/journalactivity.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/journal/journalactivity.py
@@ -520,21 +520,13 @@
     def show_main_view(self):
         if not self._init_done:
             return
+        # Only skip the rebuild when MAIN is already on screen. Bare
+        # '_active_view == MAIN' guards used to return here even when the
+        # canvas had never been set, so the first call left the Journal
+        # permanently blank.
         if self._active_view == JournalViews.MAIN and \
                 self.canvas == self._main_view:
             return
-        if self._active_view == JournalViews.MAIN:
-            return
-        if self._active_view == JournalViews.MAIN:
-            return
-        if self._active_view == JournalViews.MAIN:
-            return
-        if self._active_view == JournalViews.MAIN:
-            return
-        if self._active_view == JournalViews.MAIN:
-            return
-        if self._active_view == JournalViews.MAIN:
-            return
         self._active_view = JournalViews.MAIN
         self.project_metadata = None
         if self._editing_mode:
